  "body": "There might be a mismatch between the specification for [spec for login fallback](https://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/r0.6.1#login-fallback) and implementation(s). The specification says:\r\n\r\n> If a client does not recognize any or all login flows it can use the fallback login API:\r\n>\r\n>   GET /_matrix/static/client/login/\r\n>\r\n> This returns an HTML and JavaScript page which can perform the entire login process. The page will attempt to call the JavaScript function `window.onLogin` when login has been successfully completed.\r\n\r\nSynapse's implementation seems [to call `window.matrixLogin.onLogin`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/236d2d699d48e15d3c16ebd82dc8473a2fff8aca/synapse/static/client/login/js/login.js#L42), which is then [used by Riot iOS](https://github.com/vector-im/riot-ios/blob/bec5ed590d0330e3932df3ad110fc92ea72b84df/Riot/Modules/Home/Fallback/AuthFallBackViewController.m#L41-L47) and [Riot Android](https://github.com/vector-im/riot-android/blob/f73c3b6613bb1710d39f12a3a557dfc833ba0fa6/vector/src/main/java/im/vector/activity/FallbackAuthenticationActivity.kt#L170-L175).\r\n\r\n(Riot Web and RiotX Android don't seem to use the fallback functionality, as far as I've been able to determine.)\r\n\r\nI do not believe that Dendrite or Ruma supports fallback login. Not sure about other homeserver / client implementations. ",
